    section3Body: "Most people searching for safa tying for wedding guests in Mundra fall into one of a few groups: couples planning their own wedding, a parent or sibling handling arrangements on behalf of the groom, or a wedding planner coordinating multiple vendors for a client. Each comes to the enquiry a little differently — a couple usually already has a date and venue confirmed and just needs the safa side finalised, while a planner is often comparing vendors across several categories at once and wants a clear, fast answer on availability and pricing. Families booking on behalf of the groom sometimes reach out earlier than the groom himself would, especially when outfit shopping and safa planning happen alongside each other. Whichever category you fall into, the request is treated the same way: we ask for the date, venue, guest count and any style references, then confirm availability and recommend a package. If you're booking on someone else's behalf, it helps to loop in the groom or the couple directly once a package is being discussed, since preferences on colour and fold are usually easier to confirm with the person actually wearing the safa.",
    section4Title: "What's included and how pricing works",
